### Page 3 of 7

```text
Ciiys Origina’
LEASE
, (6f t)/o
CITY CONTRACT #5939
This Lease is made this
20th
day of
December
, 2012, between the City
of Cheyenne, a municipal corporation organized under the laws of the State of Wyoming, 2101
O’Neil Avenue, Cheyenne, Wyoming $2001 (“City”), and The Lamar Companies, a corporation
organized and existing under the laws of the State of Delaware, 5321 Corporate Blvd., Baton
Rouge, Louisiana 70808 (“Lessee”).
SECTION ONE
DESCRIPTION OF PROPERTY; TERM
In consideration of the rent provided for in Section Two of this Lease, City leases to
Lessee real property belonging to City located in Laramie County, Wyoming, and more
particularly described as a site for the placement of three billboard advertising signs described as
billboard 84-603 measuring not more than 40 feet in length by 10 feet in height located
approximately 15.5 miles West of Junction 1-25 and 1-80 on the South side of 1-80; billboard 84-
604 measuring not more than 28 feet in length by 10 feet in height located approximately 16
miles West of Junction 1-25 and 1-80 on the South side of 1-80 and billboard 84-614 measuring
not more than 30 feet in length and 10 feet in height located approximately 2.7 miles West of
Cheyenne, Wyoming, for a term of five (5) years beginning on the date that this Lease is fully
executed by the parties. That date shall be hereinafter referred to as the “commencement date.”
The advertising sign site is hereinafter referred to as the “leased property.”
SECTION TWO
RENT
Lessee shall pay City an annual rent of One Thousand Seven Hundred Dollars
($1,700.00), including $700 for billboard 84-603, $500 for billboard 84-604 and $500 for
billboard 84-614, payable within thirty (30) days after the commencement date, and payable in
advance on the commencement date in each year thereafter for the entire tern of this Lease.
SECTION THREE
USE OF PROPERTY
Lessee shall use the leased property for the construction and maintenance of three
billboards as described in Section One above, and for no other purpose whatsoever. Lessee shall
not place on the leased property any advertisement for alcohol or tobacco products.
SECTION FOUR
COMPLIANCE WITH LAW
in its use of the leased property, Lessee shall fully comply with all applicable federal,
state, county and municipal statutes, rules, regulations, and ordinances.
In its use of the leased
property, Lessee shall secure from the proper authorities all required licenses and permits before
commencing any construction, re-construction, or significant repair ofthe billboard.
SECTION FIVE
REPAIRS AND MAINTENANCE
Lessee shall, at all times during the term of this Lease, keep all improvements placed by
Lessee on the leased property in good repair, and shall maintain them at all times in a clean and
attractive condition. Construction and maintenance activities shall be conducted in a manner that
is not hazardous to livestock, including the installation of fencing if necessary to prevent
unreasonable risks of harm to livestock.
Lessee shall be responsible for any and all livestock
injuries and deaths caused or in any way resulting from construction or maintenance activities.
