SECTION SIX
INSURANCE
Lessee shall obtain, and keep in full force and effect at all times during the term of this
Lease, the following specified insurance coverages for the protection of City and Lessee against
liability arising out of the condition of the leased property, the improvements erected on the
property, or any operations of Lessee conducted pursuant to this Lease.
In the event Lessee
retains independent contractors to perform any operations on City land pursuant to this Lease,
the insurance requirements stated in this Section shall also apply to each and every such
contractor.
Commercial General Liabifity Insurance
for claims arising out of bodily injury, illness or death, or from damage to or destruction
of property of others, including loss or use thereof, with minimum limits of $1,000,000.00 per
occurrence, $2,000,000.00 aggregate for the entire term of this Lease.
Business Automobile Insurance
Including owned, non-owned and hired vehicles with minimum limits for bodily injury
and property daniage of $1,000,000.00 per accident for the entire term of this Lease.
Workers’ Compensation
Workers’ Compensation coverage shall be in effect for the entire term ofthe
Lease, as required by Wyoming law, for all employees or agents providing services under this
Lease.
Lessee shall provide the City with proof ofworkers’ compensation or employer’s
liability insurance coverage.
